hnic minority. Officially a secular state, Turkey has a Muslim-majority population. Ankara is Turkey's capital and second-largest city. Istanbul is its largest city and economic center. Other major cities include İzmir, Bursa, and Antalya.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"TR"},{"title":"Iraq","extract":"Iraq, officially the Republic of Iraq, is a country in West Asia. Located within the Middle East, it is bordered by Saudi Arabia to the south, Turkey to the north, Iran to the east, the Persian Gulf and Kuwait to the southeast, Jordan to the southwest, and Syria to the west. The country covers an area of 438,317 square kilometres (169,235 sq mi) and has a population of over 46 million, making it the 58th largest country by area and the 31st most populous in the world. Baghdad, home to over 8 million people, is the capital city and the largest in the country.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IQ"}],"arc":{"reports":2,"first_seen":"2026-10-20T12:46:26Z","first_title":"Turkish think tank urges interest rate pause amid fund crisis","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"Turkish Minute","earlier":[{"id":"e_e427d61794e7","title":"Turkish think tank urges interest rate pause amid fund crisis","date":"2026-10-20T12:46:26Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"Turkish Minute","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_703182054ed1","title":"Central Bank of Türkiye rate decision: economists expect cut to 36%","date":"2026-10-22T09:13:00Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiVEFVX3lxTE5CY0FFYnVGelNwdlVpRU1qeDBkVGZpT2otMFNrTDlfTnBYenNvS3BLb2lRbmFycklZOThyUUVNMmdYQkRpeFd1N1NtNmQwZjMxNC14RQ?oc=5","publisher":"AzerNews","verification":"single_source_report"}],"weekly":[["2026-10-19",2]],"window_days":45}}}